From 68182c8414b0c4976e7252883555541904d97780 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 07:03:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 19/20] avutil/ppc: fix wrong sel_hi permute in av_tx fft4_vec

The sel_hi constant selected words {w3,w1,w1,w3} of the z23 vector
instead of {w2,w1,w1,w2}: lanes 0 and 3 of the fft4 mid-vector read
src[3].im where src[3].re belongs, and src[3].re was never read at
all. Since fft4_vec is the recursion base of every codelet in this
file, all sizes produced wrong output (errors around 40% of peak
magnitude at every length).

This was never caught because the codelets are registered
FF_TX_PRESHUFFLE-only, so they are selected as SUB-transforms of the
generic C wrappers (fft_float_c, mdct_inv_float_c, ...). checkasm's
av_tx test compares top-level function pointers, and the top-level
stays the same C wrapper whether the sub-transform is C or AltiVec --
so it reported "no tests to perform" while the broken kernels were in
fact live in any AAC/AC3/Opus/Vorbis-style MDCT path on AltiVec.

Derived the correct selects from ff_tx_fft4_ns in tx_template.c:
tb must be {r2+r3, i2+i3, i2-i3, r3-r2}; with sel_lo = {w0,w3,w3,w0}
and VPM = {1,1,-1,-1} that requires sel_hi = {w2,w1,w1,w2}. The
remaining kernels (bf_transform vs BUTTERFLIES/CMUL, fft8_vec,
fft16_vec chain/twiddle order, sr_combine cos/sin indexing including
the v2 sine wrap) were re-derived by hand against tx_template.c and
are correct.

Validated under qemu -cpu 7400 against the pure-C planner end to end:
FFT lens 4..131072 fwd+inv and iMDCT lens 32..8192 now match C within
a few ULPs (was: FAIL at every size). A follow-up commit adds
directly-selectable top-level codelets so checkasm can actually see
and test the AltiVec path.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011BUPvhbJmFUU7zpuZf36JZ
---
 libavutil/ppc/tx_float_altivec.c | 9 +++++----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libavutil/ppc/tx_float_altivec.c b/libavutil/ppc/tx_float_altivec.c
index d3801e0..a892012 100644
--- a/libavutil/ppc/tx_float_altivec.c
+++ b/libavutil/ppc/tx_float_altivec.c
@@ -70,10 +70,11 @@ static const vuc dup_c1  = {  8,  9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14, 15,
 /* {b[0], a[3], a[2], a[1]} - reversed-sine gather for the combine pass */
 static const vuc srev    = { 16, 17, 18, 19, 12, 13, 14, 15,
                               8,  9, 10, 11,  4,  5,  6,  7 };
-/* fft4 mid-vector pair selects: {r3,i2,i2,r3} and {r2,i3,i3,r2}, so that
- * H + L gives {t6,t5} and H - L gives {t7,t8} in the right lane order */
-static const vuc sel_hi  = { 12, 13, 14, 15,  4,  5,  6,  7,
-                              4,  5,  6,  7, 12, 13, 14, 15 };
+/* fft4 mid-vector pair selects: {r3,i2,i2,r3} (words {w2,w1,w1,w2}) and
+ * {r2,i3,i3,r2} (words {w0,w3,w3,w0}), so that lo*{1,1,-1,-1} + hi yields
+ * tb = {r2+r3, i2+i3, i2-i3, r3-r2} in the lane order fft4_vec needs */
+static const vuc sel_hi  = {  8,  9, 10, 11,  4,  5,  6,  7,
+                              4,  5,  6,  7,  8,  9, 10, 11 };
 static const vuc sel_lo  = {  0,  1,  2,  3, 12, 13, 14, 15,
                              12, 13, 14, 15,  0,  1,  2,  3 };
 
